rained helmet clearance for the anthropometric template and all team drivers in the selected bracing configuration.','unresolved_decisions':['Hoop geometry, brace direction, bend nodes, attachment type and driver envelopes TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['F.7.8'],'source_clauses':[['F.5.6.1:p001','ade505b1486d1d6a32d22611ca72b3c6752ecce417a192a880769ad23fee82e3'],['F.5.6.2:p001','a2950445487be986dd5f16a8bc52708af751c41309a67575b5bfcf42a1b2419e'],['F.5.6.3:p001','94f7eaab30ecc89784bf2df3c09de23b512132aa64f82d8bb115da24c3965e22'],['F.5.6.3:p002','3e8b0fa4014c382a2ff014802ac8ea879e0ab8bd67d980bffd499fd0fd2bb7f3'],['F.5.6.3:p003','d3a317851eaa1e8bee8c960ba0f6c39b4305c9230ab2e97a51a849b9720e3ba9'],['F.5.6.4:p001','01f51b7b932dcfdd6925a078df619eba515d73b78e156740347c8e4bdd452cc6'],['F.5.6.4:p002','0322e1ccfc334478214f3ea7a8286293a1aec5b55a94a95fe360d7c66150a1fa'],['F.5.6.4:p003','8e89bb4d9da5eba0c00b8d43cc8fb957c9babb9d273fe182c63ad03175f61558'],['F.5.6.4:p004','f63c43c4c1e2e5ae03387936762e76569c26e52ef2b26c2c959ed2608bbdcda1'],['F.5.6.4:p005','6b336fd61faf1e9a2064bd13eddb95ae438d45f48c390864c097a7abda8c6d84']]],['key':'DRIVER-TEMPLATE','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:DRIVER-TEMPLATE','title':'Use the prescribed template and inspection position','model_keys':['accommodate','rollover','head'],'statement':'Represent hips/buttocks and shoulder/cervical regions by two 200 mm circles and helmeted head by a 300 mm circle, with tangent neck lines. Centers of the 200 mm circles are 490 mm apart; shoulder-to-head centers are 280 mm apart. Place the seat rearmost and pedals most forward; the lower-circle center is at least 915 mm from the pedals\' rearmost face, the middle circle rests on the seat back and the head circle is no more than 25 mm from the head restraint in the driving helmet location.','conditions_and_alternatives':['This inspection template does not replace the full required driver population.'],'verification_obligation':'Construct and dimension-check the prescribed template. Record its placement with seat/pedal extremes and verify 915 mm minimum and 25 mm maximum gaps before evaluating helmet geometry.','unresolved_decisions':['Seat/pedal adjustment ranges, head-restraint adjustment and physical template evidence TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':[],'source_clauses':[['F.5.6.5:p001','0ffd1ecebcb518a4b80847e49a1a55c6d8320d94f4cfbb5fff755bd9d93e8349'],['F.5.6.5:p002','bf871c2ac246d5a65277a15e62ef3671090d9dec67e2c684006a21a0848741bb'],['F.5.6.5:p003','3e24892fee94ce94046a11a403b8808ae3a3297b16f53eb664f57c2927a5ae92'],['F.5.6.5:p004','9a613915c8fd632ae4943cdbaa3d6347ffa8c167981319a2bd0f03ac64311d19'],['F.5.6.5:p005','e0432ceb4427288196d26b493e3b93a5fa490960724920943706ba1e47f67ab2'],['F.5.6.5:p006','034ab39dffa1749f9fd245d4f68b5909e1cb2307085b31f715e716b845f4146b'],['F.5.6.5:p007','5711dceaf841cb99bb688202852145f2d81d47fc12b5e29fb82717750764f1ae'],['F.5.6.5:p008','d3d19224900eb8d0497f41411d1bf8783e2c76a648b82c454d7feeb90e22062d'],['F.5.6.6:p001','398075d12a6911cb4e4245f16459e738134ee4b982e8ed997bcf0e3eb2f69be5'],['F.5.6.6:p002','529c357cfbebf1f2c51ca7ade23293775a4478e47a3653bc02c65a56f0214a94'],['F.5.6.6:p003','d2e8555b72a6325dfb04a0b98b4fd48e7ae92b3ce38c00a607e8b1cdc0198ccd'],['F.5.6.6:p004','d67fa6b9f2130d30fd58d54a741d45c9bb827683b46138b44b538f4f19618635'],['F.5.6.6:p005','3d565efdd960690fcd540768d46af46f03932866bbfb156264debc7b5576431a'],['F.5.6.6:p006','f2134a4f77cff919c98a3534c553e8559acc4bd13f2e654f31e1527a9a96d945'],['F.5.6.6:p007','de715a08d67a56b9052540e7ca05b048785ee2c2e976b726b45ec3a4bf66d277']]],['key':'FRONT-HOOP','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:FRONT-HOOP','title':'Constrain front-hoop material and geometry','model_keys':['rollover','accommodate'],'statement':'Use closed metal tubing of the prescribed class for a front hoop running up from the bottom frame member on one side and down to the bottom member on the other. Multiple pieces require correct triangulation. Its top is at least as high as the steering-wheel top in every angular position. Its rear surface is at most 250 mm forward of the wheel rim\'s forwardmost surface, measured horizontally on centerline with steering straight. Above the upper side-impact structure, side-view inclination is strictly below 20 degrees from vertical. A nonsteel hoop has an accessible 4 mm inspection hole. Avoid concave top-perimeter sections as the source recommendation.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Front hoop material remains unselected; the nonsteel inspection-hole condition is retained.'],'verification_obligation':'Inspect class/material, multi-piece triangulation and lower endpoints; sweep wheel positions, measure centerline distance and hoop inclination, and inspect the conditional hole and recommended top profile.','unresolved_decisions':['Front hoop material, tube shape and wheel/hoop layout TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':[],'source_clauses':[['F.5.7.1:p001','622e4aa61e36af07d8e78498a86c81b075d651d732944daa3334fb3194015cc4'],['F.5.7.2:p001','884df1bad1027c6ac10a7a0a04acaacf42a5ab71910d020417af8b49f056670d'],['F.5.7.3:p001','41b282684d4017985a64b6dba463551235edd7610f2761bf7f3024674ee61e29'],['F.5.7.4:p001','92103ab4af7db9ac0357cdd8cfd09fb2d3b3a05baa7a346e478894e3e770dcc7'],['F.5.7.5:p001','da815b4e41b4f13c75b831a8bab816bd6b486e6e7ef767b39c805789a7c07784'],['F.5.7.5:p002','a1d112dca84548d38fd741ca77de5ba2b40cd10c4e835c04b0d830e562418e1f'],['F.5.7.6:p001','876c87dc3081966c7feb31ae2114a21e95d01cc65fd6064ca790190a0aa6f867'],['F.5.7.7:p001','482c4155dd54c5ac60d8e0ca825f99a64177e6019c99cbd5e439d555c141448b'],['F.5.7.8:p001','ca1a4ed550232b61a7483f3941cb7aedfa27eabf249939fe46bf42ad3337b850']]],['key':'MAIN-HOOP','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:MAIN-HOOP','title':'Provide the continuous steel main hoop and its bracing','model_keys':['rollover','loadpath'],'statement':'Make the main hoop one uncut continuous closed steel tube of class A, spanning the lowest frame members or monocoque bottom. Above the upper side-impact attachment its side-view inclination is strictly below 10 degrees from vertical; below it, forward inclination is unrestricted but rearward inclination is at most 10 degrees. At the bottom-major-structure attachments, front-view inside spacing is at least 380 mm. Provide left and right straight, unbent closed steel class B braces: forward when the hoop leans forward, rearward when it leans rearward, either direction if vertical. Attach no more than 160 mm below the hoop top, preferably as near its top as possible, at an included angle of at least 30 degrees. Securely integrate braces to carry all hoop loads to the major structure without failure.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Mandatory steel applications cannot be replaced with the permitted aluminum alternatives for other members.'],'verification_obligation':'Inspect continuous steel construction, class and brace count; measure angles, spacing and attachment height. Substantiate integration and full load transfer using the applicable chassis/bracing support and joint rules.','unresolved_decisions':['Main hoop/brace geometry, joining method, support design and load evidence TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['F.6.6','F.7.7','F.5.12','F.5.13'],'source_clauses':[['F.5.8.1:p001','d97ea2188cb5cbae251e22eeb7218088e345dbe7db17c18b5d201acd4517ea7f'],['F.5.8.2:p001','6b772e349807830bea6514c4c47d1c3172f90dc478c308ae20f05094f87a3041'],['F.5.8.3:p001','03a23996fd49d55f4c01fbb342958eb4ca4a39d2653fada39a76d7c416a6527a'],['F.5.8.3:p002','345fd6c362c26f8388831d2e20daae1abf194dd5c40f1b62a1bd4647ab2bd7e7'],['F.5.8.3:p003','f2d3a8731fecf2f85988b539f150a90bfb9d79104e558bff5f9ce323ecb2ee6c'],['F.5.8.3:p004','420ffa10acf360addfe196d3c8d779653eb54cc103e86a052d1acabc2ddced74'],['F.5.8.3:p005','952d1a66c6a21aaf763c7be48eef4e45a330574283872313cd77715defe54c1e'],['F.5.8.4:p001','2e8eace98ef881b456d511609b4d1d22b31fd6ffefc5c3d496bc63e2cd3221dd'],['F.5.9.1:p001','511984706ae93ef32e3e69afb3781fa9c2f7d9650521cb35b602537a61f5e53a'],['F.5.9.2:p001','