; measure the complete upper-edge band, hoop connections and bay triangulation for each side.','unresolved_decisions':['Chassis construction, side-impact member sections, bends and nodes TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':[],'source_clauses':[['F.6.4.1:p001','53847475b94a226205cf5ecb1f89187653edd6a833a08770579018e52980209c'],['F.6.4.2:p001','54c8a9af8a57f01f2476ce0962ff03179a95af7369a035806fcf4ea8fa70b2d3'],['F.6.4.3:p001','79f8c3f6e1f773d04187e0ae2751b90bbb60a5ab2149ca7322ac97c8b146a7f2'],['F.6.4.4:p001','4a62f9da1b252a12e824eab8e8bd3b8f6abf34690a6269f312587a1359ebb190'],['F.6.4.4:p002','4b0b6c419d74d913142f2fba51ee5d218ab7a6f9f6ac5cd19bdbfdaa10ae9381'],['F.6.4.4:p003','a6a8a232b084e02c150159209e3be7f533901a600054f5f6e059ee85212cae57'],['F.6.4.5:p001','87d345f7d30a86255a35f6dcc6494af635869b6fb27419e7d46a84bd3ad9df6c'],['F.6.4.6:p001','3999ef7659f96fcf4c76dc48011c9b86f760dd15ad5341b73cd21591b7507186'],['F.6.4.6:p002','889bb8d4e998405e1223cf96e687a0219b8e917ced561c0f9f12aa4fe1d13bcf'],['F.6.4.6:p003','1c42da888270e6532300e42307a56244806a3c6ac479e15a45dd7244ff7c0daf']]],['key':'SIDE-MONOCOQUE','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:SIDE-MONOCOQUE','title':'Retain monocoque side-impact equivalence and physical tests','model_keys':['side','loadpath'],'statement':'For a monocoque define the side-impact zone between hoops as at least 290 mm of vertical height above the floor bottom plus half the horizontal floor. Establish equivalence to three class B steel tubes. The vertical portion from floor bottom to 345 mm above the floor\'s lowest bottom point is equivalent to at least two class B steel tubes and has no side-view openings between hoops. Calculate horizontal-floor equivalence under F.4.3. For a 25 mm-diameter laminate section show perimeter shear of at least 7.5 kN by the F.4.2.5 physical test and include results in the SES.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Conditional monocoque alternative; no fabricated laminate strength is asserted.'],'verification_obligation':'Review the selected side/floor geometry and F.4.3 equivalence calculations, inspect absence of vertical-side openings and obtain the specified laminate perimeter-shear test/SES records.','unresolved_decisions':['Laminate/core geometry, equivalence data, coupons and SES evidence TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['F.4.2.5','F.4.3'],'source_clauses':[['F.7.5.1:p001','8d733acf6585cd1b96ba01757c4d1fca2e03b72da2fd755082e61822c93a5148'],['F.7.5.2:p001','a7cf84eb0e1f4b19f7c2ebd87357523f3c6f75a1b0ece08c305e07f34a7b13f6'],['F.7.5.3:p001','c8339d161ddfe38a9614807d8373e1e2a0bee9b018d8c66a4daaf83fd14cee27'],['F.7.5.3:p002','56d12946b0d00899d7b408b658a369e12b22debd8b65e90091b7f13c4afdd2de'],['F.7.5.3:p003','211f07a6a47ebd90bc8e4700f8c92a957c702f951e4a31229f6286a46ef607e6'],['F.7.5.4:p001','28101ddca6a2df61be6c891bf6fc78f9c37af5f7c13c6c4a8e616428e4ec0ef5'],['F.7.5.5:p001','35c0aa14ba3beb1565770adddca2ced92afe4627fb5894cdbb7882b69ae5f41a'],['F.7.5.5:p002','9a7e06c49c9cc3a34a06b46751bf0f4224f16a761e74b77ab80aea18319807ac']]],['key':'FRONT-STACK','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:FRONT-STACK','title':'Place the attenuator and AIP in a protected load path','model_keys':['front','loadpath'],'statement':'Locate the impact attenuator ahead of the front bulkhead with an anti-intrusion plate between them. Both attenuator-to-AIP and AIP-to-bulkhead attachments carry transverse and vertical loads from off-axis impacts.','conditions_and_alternatives':['All attenuator/AIP construction and attachment variants.'],'verification_obligation':'Review the physical stack and establish transverse/vertical load paths at both attachments under off-axis impact cases.','unresolved_decisions':['Front bulkhead, AIP, attenuator and off-axis load-path design TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':[],'source_clauses':[['F.8.1.1:p001','eacef5c047af5c16cf13717585a3d8c7374e9f91decb5368a435240bdf6cfab6'],['F.8.1.2:p001','7d79b36763613bab5aad6589a4a5051ac476e2a6914a84a81463104c069febea']]],['key':'AIP','identifier':'FSAE2027:VP:obligation:AIP','title':'Retain AIP material and attachment alternatives','model_keys':['front','loadpath'],'statement':'Choose a solid steel AIP at least 1.5 mm thick, solid aluminum at least 4.0 mm thick, or a composite meeting F.8.3. For welding, the profile reaches or exceeds the bulkhead tube centerline on every side; for bolting/bonding/laminating it reaches or exceeds the complete outer bulkhead periphery. Document direct attachment in SES. Weld lengths are at least 25 mm with interrupted weld/space ratio at least 1:1. Bolting uses at least eight critical fasteners at least 8 mm or 5/16 in diameter, with bolt centers at least 50 mm apart, and 15 kN pullout/bending capacity per attachment. Tearout is 15 kN per bolt or total mounting tearout exceeds the F.8.5.3.b attenuator attachment strength. Bonding requires no bulkhead openings, bonding over the AIP\'s entire surface and shear/peel strengths strictly above 120 kN. Laminating places the AIP ahead of the outer bulkhead skin, encloses it fully and provides shear capability strictly above 120 kN.','conditions_and_alternatives':['Material and attachment alternatives are constraints awaiting a decision, not multiple simultaneously selected designs.'],'verification_obligation':'Select material/attachment, measure the corresponding profile/thickness/fastener/weld geometry and substantiate conditional strength and SES documentation for the selected method. Record the rejected alternatives with rationale.','unresolved_decisions':['AIP material, dimensions and attachment method TBD.'],'dependent_source_rules':['T.8.2','F.8.5.3'],'source_clauses':[['F.8.2.1:p001','833284f1a68a3046bbe112913fe410708c8b84cba691f51ee776980d65f56180'],['F.8.2.1:p002','010eaf49cf769c9d9fd7b3160193a1aa6328a087203a31f43cb9bcec68d18d18'],['F.8.2.1:p003','6b3d3f3f3630220fa8b2d54048f6cfdbe1797845daacedc765846ef5a4e57632'],['F.8.2.1:p004','7b0e5ed6affd18b5ac540ec8cdf9d38f1065840d1c78f756659a17b4d6a62e1f'],['F.8.2.2:p001','1de2ad6792bf86d7048edea